│ patch_description        │ Remove the globally shared pre/post RZ rotations, which commute with the CZ network and   │
│                          │ add two parameters without providing wire-specific control. Retain the two parity-shared  │
│                          │ RY parameters and strengthen feature mixing with a parameter-free multiscale CZ graph: a  │
│                          │ periodic nearest-neighbor ring captures local structure, while four opposite-wire         │
│                          │ couplings propagate information across the full register. This reduces the distinct       │
│                          │ ansatz parameters from four to two, lowers the train-test overfitting opportunity, and    │
│                          │ adds long-range interactions aimed at improving worst-group separation.                   │
