│ patch_description        │ This replaces the deep ring-based rotation circuit with a compact QAOA-style ansatz.      │
│                          │ Commuting ZZ interactions connect qubits through the three perfect matchings of a         │
│                          │ 3-dimensional hypercube, allowing information to propagate globally with low depth. All   │
│                          │ interactions share one parameter, while all RY mixers share a second parameter. This      │
│                          │ strong parameter tying acts as regularization for the small training set, reduces the     │
│                          │ train-validation gap, and should converge faster while retaining substantially richer     │
│                          │ nonlocal correlations than the previous CZ ring.                                          │
