│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_mix_midrange                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses three distinct rotation parameters, 28 gates per block, and an    │
│                          │ effective depth of 15. Its parity-specific rotations and final mixer provide reasonable   │
│                          │ validation margin, but parameter efficiency is low. The new configuration regularizes all │
│                          │ rotations with one shared parameter while retaining alternating RX/RY axes for            │
│                          │ parity-sensitive transformations. It adds a parameter-free mid-range CZ layer between     │
│                          │ local and antipodal connectivity, creating local, medium-range, and global correlation    │
│                          │ scales. This keeps the effective depth at approximately 15 while reducing the distinct    │
│                          │ parameter count from three to one, which should improve parameter efficiency, few-shot    │
│                          │ generalization, and worst-group separation. Training settings such as learning rate and   │
│                          │ iteration count are fixed externally and therefore unchanged.                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
