│ patch_description        │ Insert a complementary shared-angle rotation layer between the antipodal CZ links and the │
│                          │ local brickwork. Because CZ gates mutually commute, merely reordering the existing        │
│                          │ entanglers does not create a meaningfully different unitary. The intermediate RX/RY layer │
│                          │ makes the global-first ordering operationally distinct, allowing antipodal correlations   │
│                          │ to be remixed before local propagation. All rotations reuse the existing parameter,       │
│                          │ preserving the single-distinct-parameter regularization that favors small-data            │
│                          │ generalization.                                                                           │
